<!-- Section 1: The Anchor — Platform Explainer -->
<section class="pa-hero">
  <div class="pa-hero-text">
    <div class="pa-kicker">Our Inquiry</div>
    <h1 class="pa-hero-title">It's time we asked the question: <em>What is the point of Scotland being in the union?</em></h1>
    <p class="pa-body">Is there a point?</p>
    <p class="pa-body">We know why Scotland's in the union — the UK. We were forced into it. Or tricked, if you prefer. One thing's for sure — we didn't march into it on 1 May 1707 singing and dancing in a big parade.</p>
    <p class="pa-body">So if there is a point to Scotland being in the union, then it had better be a good one.</p>
    <p class="pa-body">The union affects Scotland every day, in every way, in every part of our lives. In our electricity bills. In our fishing waters. In decisions made by governments we didn't elect, about weapons we didn't ask for, stored in waters we live beside.</p>
    <p class="pa-closing">If the union is affecting our lives and our futures every day, shouldn't we ask: <em>what is the point of Scotland being in the union?</em></p>
  </div>
  <figure class="pa-hero-image" aria-hidden="true"></figure>
</section>

